Byte-by-byte Description of file: table.dat
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   Bytes Format Units   Label     Explanations
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
   1- 10  A10   ---     Star      Star name
  12- 13  I2    h       RAh       Right ascension (J2000.0)
  15- 16  I2    min     RAm       Right ascension (J2000.0)
  18- 22  F5.2  s       RAs       Right ascension (J2000.0)
      24  A1    ---     DE-       Declination sign (J2000.0)
  25- 26  I2    deg     DEd       Declination (J2000.0)
  28- 29  I2    arcmin  DEm       Declination (J2000.0)
  31- 34  F4.1  arcsec  DEs       Declination (J2000.0)
  36- 45  A10   ---     SpType    MK Spectral type
  48- 52  I5    K       Teff      ? Effective temperature
  54- 57  F4.2  [cm/s2] log(g)    ? Gravity surface
  59- 63  F5.2  [Sun]   [Fe/H]    ? Metallicity
  65- 70  F6.3  mag     VMAG      ? Absolute visual magnitude
  72- 75  F4.2  mag   E_VMAG      ? Error on absolute magnitude (upper limit)
  79- 82  F4.2  mag   e_VMAG      ? Error on absolute magnitude (lower limit)
  85- 88  F4.2  mag     Av        ? Absorption
  90-118  A29   ---     OName     Other identifications
 120-122  A3    ---     Add       [Add ] Indicates additional stars not
                                         presented in the paper
 124-143  A20   ---     cSpFile1  Spectrum file in "cor_sp" subdirectory (1)
 145-165  A21   ---     oSpFile1  Spectrum file in "obs_sp" subdirectory (2)
 167-186  A20   ---     cSpFile2  Spectrum file in "cor_sp" subdirectory (1)
 188-208  A21   ---     oSpFile2  Spectrum file in "obs_sp" subdirectory (2)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Note (1): Spectra corrected for interstellar extinction and radial velocity.
    The fluxes in the FITS files are expressed in 10mW/m2/nm (erg/cm2/s/{AA})
Note (2): fluxes expressed in 10mW/m2/nm (erg/cm2/s/{AA})
